Question 3

Blogging Platform

Admin role who can manage users and moderate posts/comments.
Registered User: Can create blog posts and leave comments on any post.

main actions users can take in the app:

Posts
A user can create a blog post with a title and body.

A user can view all blog posts on a homepage.

A user can view a detailed page for a single post.

A user can edit or delete their own posts.

Comments

A user can add comments to any post.

A user can see all comments on a post.

A user can delete their own comments.

Example User Flow
A user signs up or logs in.

They land on a homepage that lists recent blog posts.

They can click a post to read it fully and see comments.

They can write their own post, or comment on another post.

They can go to their dashboard to manage their own posts.

Possible Data Models
User: name, email, password_digest
→ has_many :posts
→ has_many :comments

Post: title, body, user_id
→ belongs_to :user
→ has_many :comments

Comment: body, user_id, post_id
→ belongs_to :user
→ belongs_to :post

Question 4

ERD
1. Users

Table name: users
Columns:

id (primary key)

name (string)

email (string, unique)

password_digest (string, for secure passwords via has_secure_password)

created_at (datetime)

updated_at (datetime)

Associations:

has_many :posts

has_many :comments

2. Posts

Table name: posts
Columns:

id (primary key)

title (string)

body (text)

user_id (foreign key)

created_at (datetime)

updated_at (datetime)

Associations:

belongs_to :user

has_many :comments

 3. Comments
 
Table name: comments
Columns:

id (primary key)

body (text)

user_id (foreign key)

post_id (foreign key)

created_at (datetime)

updated_at (datetime)

Associations:

belongs_to :user

belongs_to :post

Relationships Summary
A User has many Posts

A User has many Comments

A Post belongs to a User

A Post has many Comments

A Comment belongs to a User

A Comment belongs to a Post


